{
  "_notes": [
    "Big Bang Bar (Capcom 1996)",
    "Capcom 16-bit bus: 8-bit NVRAM data on D0-D7, actual data at even file positions",
    "CPU address = 0x30000000 + even_index * 2",
    "High scores stored as score/10 (scale: 10)",
    "Small scores (regular, elite, weak kidney) stored as integers with scale 1",
    "The BBB 1.9 ROM's game-over path reads each full 32-bit score from player structures based at 0x00061F1C (0x70-byte stride), offset +0x16: 0x00061F32, 0x00061FA2, 0x00062012, 0x00062082. The same values are passed to the decimal formatter and final-score NVRAM writer.",
    "These logical MC68306 addresses require a bus-correct PinmameReadMainCPUByte implementation using cpunum_read_byte(); the former memory_get_read_ptr() implementation returned raw host-layout bytes and produced patterned garbage.",
    "Recent-game scores are verified persistent NVRAM values stored as score/10."
  ],
  "_fileformat": 0.8,
  "_metadata": {
    "version": 9,
    "copyright": [
